OracleAdapter.setManualPrice

when called by the owner with a valid token and non-zero price and after the interval
    it updates manualPrices[token] to the new price
        expect manualPrices[token] to equal the new price
    it updates manualLastUpdated[token] to block.timestamp
        expect manualLastUpdated[token] to equal block.timestamp (≈ within 1s tolerance)
    it emits ManualPriceUpdated event with correct parameters
        expect event with (token, price, timestamp == block.timestamp)

when updating an existing token price after the interval
    it overwrites the previous price and updates the timestamp
        expect new price and newer timestamp

when called before lastUpdated + manualUpdateInterval
    it reverts
        expect revert with EarlyManualUpdate

when token is the zero address
    it reverts
        expect revert with ZeroAddress

when price is zero
    it reverts
        expect revert with ZeroAmount

when called by a non-owner
    it reverts
        expect revert with OwnableUnauthorizedAccount and the caller address
